# C051 BUILD #8 — THE ENV LIFECYCLE: secrets in .env (temp preflight), non-secrets in the manifest (2026-07-01; operator:
# ".env.temp with the minimum keys that gets deleted after a proper .env exists; an example created if we run without it"
# + "non secrets should be defined in platform.config.ts"). The generator now splits config by SENSITIVITY, both driven
# from platform.config.ts: (1) SECRETS (BETTER_AUTH_SECRET, STRIPE_SECRET_KEY, STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET required; RESEND/GOOGLE
# optional) -> a generated `.env.example` (required uncommented, optional commented, NO values — safe to commit) + a
# generated `scripts/env-check.ts` PREFLIGHT wired as `predev`/`check`: if a required secret is missing (checking .env AND
# process.env), it WRITES .env.temp from the example + reports the missing keys + fails (exit 1); once .env has EVERY
# required secret it DELETES .env.temp. So an example appears the moment you try to run without one, and is cleaned up once
# provisioned — TESTED both directions (no-.env -> .env.temp created + exit 1; .env with the 3 secrets -> .env.temp deleted +
# exit 0). (2) NON-SECRETS (BASE_URL/EMAIL_FROM/TRUSTED_ORIGINS/ENVIRONMENT/STRIPE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY/BETTER_AUTH_URL) -> a new
# manifest `vars` field -> generated into `wrangler.toml [vars]` (unset ones commented with a hint); wrangler.toml MERGES so
# provisioned binding ids survive a regen. The CATALOG gained per-service `env` metadata (name/required/secret/hint);
# collectEnv unions it. Also generates `.gitignore` — MERGE-aware (a SAFETY FIX: an app's minimal .gitignore would else
# leave .env UNIGNORED -> risk of committing secrets; now the standard ignores are appended, never skipped) + wires
# dev/deploy/check scripts + the wrangler devDep. platform tests 26 pass. autotoolfactory: manifest vars moved to `vars` ->
# wrangler [vars] populated; .env.example + env-check + .gitignore generated; tsc 0 own-code errors; .env/.env.temp ignored
# (autotoolfactory 0be6310). @suluk/platform 0.1.9 (env) + 0.1.10 (the .gitignore-merge safety fix). So platform.config.ts
# remains the ONLY hand-authored surface, with SECRETS the only thing supplied outside it (via .env, never committed).
claim platform_c051_build8_env_lifecycle_secrets_dotenv_temp_nonsecrets_manifest_vars: Bool @>=0.6 = True
falsified_when platform_c051_build8_env_lifecycle_secrets_dotenv_temp_nonsecrets_manifest_vars == False

# C055 — ENCRYPTED-COMMITTED .env via @suluk/env (2026-07-01, operator: "env should be encrypted and decrypted like
