# its secret VALUES ENCRYPTED (@suluk/env post-quantum ML-KEM-768 + AES-256-GCM, dotenvx's commit-safely model); only the
# PRIVATE key (SULUK_PRIVATE_KEY / .env.keys) stays out of git. The generator emits: (1) src/env.ts — a @suluk/env defineEnv
# DECLARE-ONCE for the app's secrets (from the catalog metadata; each surfaces:["cloudflare"]); (2) the .env COMMITTED with
# values encrypted (operator: suluk-env keygen -> set; the generator writes a values-free scaffold ONLY IF ABSENT so a regen
