# C056 — PROVISIONING ENV COMPLETENESS + the EPHEMERAL-MASTER credential lifecycle (2026-07-01, operator across 5 turns:
# "autotoolfactory has less env vars than toolfactory — we didn't provision properly" -> ".env.temp plaintext -> encrypt to
# .env, delete provisioning-only creds before push" -> "provisioning consumes .env.temp if exists (deletes it) or uses
# existing .env" -> "master token not in git, only scoped tokens; decryption key -> CF worker + ~/.suluk/settings.json" ->
# "instruct user to revoke the master CF token after minting"). Grounded in a full map of toolfactory's env.ts/.env/provision/
# mint scripts (24 vars; toolfactory KEEPS all creds encrypted — we diverge to ephemeral-master). BUILT: EnvVar gains
# surface("local"|"cloudflare") + provisioning(ephemeral master, deleted before commit) + minted(scoped token). The catalog's
# `app` declares CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN (master, provisioning), CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID (keeper), scoped D1/WORKERS/KV tokens
# (minted); `admin` declares SUPERADMIN_EMAILS. src/env.ts (defineEnv) emits each with its surface. THE LIFECYCLE (generated
# scripts): .env.temp = plaintext bootstrap (gitignored); scripts/provision.ts = keygen+link-key -> source creds (CONSUME
# .env.temp if present else decrypt .env) -> suluk-provision apply -> mint-tokens (scoped from master via CF API) -> encrypt
# keepers -> DELETE the ephemeral master from .env -> rm .env.temp -> git add -f .env -> INSTRUCT operator to REVOKE the master
# in the CF dashboard. scripts/mint-tokens.ts mints the scoped tokens. The decryption key (SULUK_PRIVATE_KEY) lives in
# ~/.suluk/settings.json (local) AND is pushed to the Worker by sync-secrets (loadEnv decrypts at runtime). env-check +
# .env.example reflect the .env.temp->provision->sealed-.env flow. VERIFIED: platform 92 tests pass, tsc clean; src/env.ts
# typechecks + all 4 generated scripts (provision/mint-tokens/sync-secrets/link-key) transpile + resolve against
# @suluk/env/node in autotoolfactory. @suluk/platform 0.4.0 published. ADR C056. Ceiling 0.62: env-declaration + lifecycle
# scripts BUILT + tested, but the CF-calling steps (suluk-provision apply / token minting / wrangler secret put) are
# OPERATOR-RUN and NOT yet executed end-to-end against a real Cloudflare account (that live run is the missing witness).
claim platform_c056_provisioning_env_completeness_ephemeral_master_lifecycle_built: Bool @>=0.62 = True
falsified_when platform_c056_provisioning_env_completeness_ephemeral_master_lifecycle_built == False

# C057 — MOCK-PROVIDER LOCAL DEV (2026-07-02, operator: "allow using other providers... such that we can mock them —
# cloudflare -> local sqlite file + json KV, google -> better-auth flow that logs in any email, hyperswitch -> static
# generic responses, resend -> local sqlite/json email store, no separate runtime; then add real keys to .env.temp + run
# provision to swap to real and remove the mocks"). CLARIFIED (operator): NOT local-vs-prod environments — a SINGLE env,
# MOCK-UNTIL-KEYED: no key -> mock (temporary mock sqlite, NOT miniflare); key present (after provision) -> real. So the
# selection is env/binding-PRESENCE autodetect (the design panel's dual-entry + SULUK_LOCAL positive-signal was rejected as
# overkill — its fail-open worry assumed a separate prod env that does not exist yet; future multi-env + feature-flags is the
# proper prod-lockdown). C052 SPLIT (the operator's explicit ask): ZERO new packages — every mock extends an EXISTING owner +
# registry wiring. BUILT + PROVEN END-TO-END + PUBLISHED + LIVE-ADOPTED (autotoolfactory local:true, bun run dev): (1) a
# manifest `local: true` flag (default false -> the C051/C053 golden stays byte-identical; a companion golden locks the
# variant) makes the generator emit `src/dev.ts` — a bun server that runs the SAME wired app (index.ts gains `export const
# app`) under bun with mock bindings; the deployed Worker (src/index.ts) imports NONE of the mocks (grep-verified 0), so
# bun:sqlite never enters the bundle. (2) CLOUDFLARE: @suluk/cloudflare/local (new bun-only subpath) — d1FromSqlite (a
# D1Database facade over bun:sqlite, PROVEN against drizzle-orm/d1: insert...returning/where/update/project) + jsonFileKvStore
# (KVNamespace over JSON) + applyLocalSchema (derives CREATE TABLE DDL from the drizzle schema objects via getTableConfig —
# there are NO .sql migrations; proven creating all 22 autotoolfactory tables). (3) GOOGLE: @suluk/better-auth devLoginHandler
# — POST /api/auth/dev-login {email} mints a REAL session via the PUBLIC signUp+signIn(asResponse) API (no internal-adapter/
# cookie forging; proven: any-email login -> real session token + cookie -> get-session resolves the user). FAIL-CLOSED: the
# gate lives in the npm handler (armed flag, checked before input); registry/auth arms it only in dev-mock (ENVIRONMENT!=
# production AND no GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID) + enables email/password there. PROVEN: ENVIRONMENT=production -> 404. (4) STRIPE:
# @suluk/billing mockStripeFetch — a fetch returning generic parseable objects for every endpoint billing calls (proven
# through the real transport: createCustomer/checkout/subscription/prices); dev entry injects env.STRIPE_FETCH only when no
# real key. (5) RESEND: @suluk/email storeProvider(sink) + @suluk/cloudflare/local jsonFileMailbox — dev sends SAVE to a local
# JSON inbox (route GET /api/email/dev/mailbox); registry/email threads env.SULUK_MAILBOX_SINK. Published email@0.2.0
# cloudflare@0.3.1 billing@0.2.0 better-auth@0.2.0 platform@0.5.2. CEILING 0.8 not higher: the stripe mock is generic (not a
# stateful simulator — a webhook-driven credit grant needs the webhook fired manually) and the "local connects to REAL D1/KV
# after provision" path is DEFERRED (a bun process can't bind remote D1/KV; needs the D1 HTTP API — real HTTP providers
# Google/Stripe/Resend DO work locally post-provision via decrypted .env).
claim platform_c057_mock_provider_local_dev_autodetect_built_proven_published_adopted: Bool @>=0.8 = True
falsified_when platform_c057_mock_provider_local_dev_autodetect_built_proven_published_adopted == False
